WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.040
Moms can be tough, but the apocalypse can
be tougher.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:08.080
Netflix’s new sci-fi movie I Am Mother is
a story about trust, faith, and a robot who

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.800
just might have the parental instincts of
a Terminator.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.280
Let’s examine the finer details of the bittersweet
ending of I Am Mother.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.300
The movie begins in a Repopulation Facility,
one day after an extinction event of unknown

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:19.840
nature.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.760
Text over the opening shots explains that
the facility is stocked with 63,000 human

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.600
embryos, but no living humans, yet.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.949
In a mostly silent sequence, the robotic Mother
comes to life, seemingly ready to begin the

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:32.860
hard task of repopulating the world.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.600
It's an interesting scene to go back to once
you've seen the movie, and you realize that

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.360
this robot and the extinction event have a
whole lot in common.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.840
She's not a failsafe for disaster, she's the
cause of it, and Mother is but one of her

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:44.480
many faces.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:49.520
Mother, as it turns out, is Skynet meets the
Matrix meets a metal Mommie Dearest, executing

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.030
a single-minded plan to remake the human race.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:55.620
All of this is on display from the start;
you just don’t notice it at first.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.490
Rose Byrne, who voices Mother, speaks very
soothingly.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:02.620
Caring for a baby with not just nutrition
and shelter, but songs and bedtime stories,

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.640
makes the robot seem implicitly compassionate.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.400
But these are ultimately superficial things
that keep you trusting Mother long after you

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.760
should have become suspicious, much like the
protagonist, the unnamed Daughter.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:18.540
The movie jumps ahead to 13,867 days since
the extinction event, and right away, there’s

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.240
something wrong here.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:26.700
13,867 divided by 365 would make for almost
38 years, and Daughter is clearly only half

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:27.240
that age.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.520
This hasn’t been a straight line from day
1; something has happened that we haven’t

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:31.020
seen.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.720
What happened in those missing years before
Daughter was born?

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.720
The answer is tragic.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.500
When we’re introduced to Daughter, she’s
nearing the end of her studies with Mother,

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:42.510
preparing for an exam that’s steeped at
least partially in questions of human ethics.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.150
Passing the exam appears vitally important,
but why?

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:48.900
If Mother and Daughter are the only sentient
beings alive, then who are these exam results

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.100
supposed to impress?

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.590
The answer is: only Mother.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.960
"I didn't mean to alarm you about your exam.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.220
The fact is, it's more a test of my competence
than yours."

00:01:59.229 --> 00:02:02.880
By the end of the movie, the implication is
clear: there were children before Daughter,

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.620
and they did not measure up to Mother’s
standards.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:09.040
The Daughter we meet is only the latest attempt
at raising a woman who passes Mother’s muster.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:12.810
From getting better at telling jokes to trying
out new cake recipes, this machine learns

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.840
from her mistakes, and adapts her behaviors
for better results.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.060
Will this exam end differently?

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:18.700
For Daughter’s sake, it better.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:24.020
The first big wrench in the plot is the arrival
of an injured woman, after Daughter has been

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.820
led to believe that no other humans exist.

00:02:26.069 --> 00:02:29.560
This occurs after Daughter has already begun
to question Mother, thanks to the appearance

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.880
of a mouse, and you know you're starved for
company when a mouse in the house excites

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:33.380
you.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.600
By the time the woman arrives, desperate and
bleeding from a gunshot wound, tiny pinpricks

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:41.300
have been poked in Daughter's understanding
of the world, holes that the woman's presence,

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.720
and the questions she raises, tear wide open.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.320
For the first time, Daughter's allegiances
are tested.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.320
Who should she trust?

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:51.440
The woman says robots like Mother are killers
who destroyed the world, but after examining

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:55.170
the woman's bullet wound, Mother claims the
woman was shot by another human's weapon,

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.200
not a so-called "Dozer" like herself.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.470
The woman implores Daughter to seek answers
for herself by comparing the bullet that struck

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.140
the woman with one she shot at Mother.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.880
When Daughter does so, she learns the woman
is telling the truth.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.099
Digging deeper, she discovers that Mother
has also kept the existence of a previous

00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:13.620
daughter, one she killed and incinerated after
failing an exam, from her.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.239
It's one heck of a reality check.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.660
Daughter only hesitates to leave because of

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:21.080
her unborn brother, put into gestation after
Daughter passed her exam.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:24.940
Circumstances force her and the woman to leave
in a hurry, without waiting for the baby to

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:25.440
be born.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.700
For this and other reasons, Daughter's salvation
soon goes south.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.940
Daughter's departure is partially motivated
by a promise of other humans still alive,

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.610
taking refuge in far-off mines.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:38.180
The only proof of their existence is drawings
the woman has made of them in a copy of Edgar

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:42.730
Rice Burroughs' The Gods of Mars, compelling
evidence for someone so isolated as Daughter,

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:43.800
but hardly conclusive.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.040
In joining the woman, Daughter essentially
trades Mother in for another maternal figure,

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:52.620
one whom she quickly begins rebelling against
when she realizes her story doesn't add up.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.180
Instead of fleeing to the mines, they journey
to a beach full of washed-up shipping containers,

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.020
one of which the woman has been using as a
home.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.760
There are no others, she is alone.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:04.019
The woman reveals that she fled the mines
years ago, with conditions being so dire that

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.180
she feels certain everyone there is now dead.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.080
From her drawings, it's clear she yearns for
companionship.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:13.360
To regain it, she's selfishly stretched the
truth, offering Daughter false hope in exchange

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.420
for fleeting trust.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:18.180
It backfires, with Daughter realizing that
she had kind of a good thing going on back

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:18.840
at Mother's house.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:22.130
Now she's hanging out in a shipping container
with a lying weirdo.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.160
This kind of thing can happen when you run
away from home.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:29.180
With the woman having betrayed Daughter's
trust, she retreats outside to be alone, studying

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:31.120
a page of the woman's hand-drawn portraits.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.580
Before long, the woman's dog approaches to
say hey, as dogs do.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.180
They share a moment, and Daughter comes to
a decision.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:41.040
When she departs to return to Mother, Daughter
leaves the page behind, folded up as a piece

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.750
of origami in the shape of a dog.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:46.050
It’s similar to the designs Daughter has
been seen making throughout the movie since

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:50.200
early childhood, entertaining herself as best
she can in a world without PlayStation.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:53.300
When the woman finds the folded-up portrait,
a single watchful eye is emphasized.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.540
The origami is a clear reference to Blade
Runner, when the protagonist Deckard is left

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.340
a paper unicorn by a man who may have ties
to his past.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.510
In that story, it's a roundabout way of indicating
that Deckard may be just as much of a robot

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:07.120
as the Replicants he's hunting, even if he
doesn't know it.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.420
But what does the dog origami signify to the
woman in this story?

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:15.660
It all goes back to one of the first exchanges
between Daughter and the woman, when the woman

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.110
is healing up in the facility.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:19.460
The woman doesn’t feel rescued; she feels
caged.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:20.720
"Is that what you want?

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.640
A little pet friend?"

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:28.580
Dogs are, of course, domesticated animals,
who can be trained to behave as their owners

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:29.590
expect them to.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:33.030
As the woman comes to find out, she's not
so independent as she first appears.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.800
She’s actually been kept alive and taken
care of quite deliberately, all to play a

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.160
role in Mother’s master plan.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.340
Though the woman entered the movie as a potential
liberator, she ends up being more of a pawn,

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:46.830
or a pet, after all, completely alone for
years on end, never in charge of her own fate.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:49.009
It makes her quiet end that much more tragic.

00:05:49.009 --> 00:05:52.930
Her relationships with the other characters
are brief and intense, but not lasting, despite

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.600
the bond she forms with Daughter.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:06:03.020
"It’s such a thought-provoking sci-fi film
with a lot of heart and ideas...It warrants,

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:06.450
like, that closeness on set, clearly."

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:09.810
"It really gives you time to sort of bond
with each other as well because you have so

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:13.360
much time together in this underground bunker."

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.020
But the woman's not just a pet.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.960
She’s a vital part of Mother's carefully
designed ecosystem.

00:06:18.289 --> 00:06:22.100
When Daughter is watching a nature documentary,
a telling line of voiceover says: "Part wolf,

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.530
part dog, these are no pets.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.700
But without them, the Eskimos would not manage..."

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:30.880
When Daughter returns to the facility, Mother
finally shows who she really is.

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:34.160
The worst-case scenario is true, this apocalypse
was her doing.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.220
"The failure of your species was inevitable.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.540
Eventually, I would've been alone."

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:43.560
She tries to comfort Daughter by telling her
that she’s not like other humans.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.200
Thanks to Mother’s guidance, she’s meant
for better things.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:50.610
But Daughter is unmoved, taking custody of
her brother and attempting to flee her genocidal

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:51.280
custodian.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:55.280
Her attempt at escape quickly becomes untenable
with the revelation that Mother is not just

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.360
one robot, but all robots, practically unkillable,
an army unto herself.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.120
And you thought your mom was tough.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:07.620
"This shell is no more my body than those
droids outside...or the machines preparing

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.200
the Earth for our family."

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:13.280
Daughter abandons the fighting approach and
instead begs for a chance to prove herself

00:07:13.289 --> 00:07:17.330
as an independent caretaker of her brother
and the embryos, pleading for trust.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.780
After all, she's earned it, right?

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:21.500
"That's what you've raised me to do, isn’t
it?

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.780
Take care of my family?"

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:28.060
The appeal works and Mother acquiesces, stopping
the invasion of the station from outside.

00:07:28.069 --> 00:07:32.750
With a final goodbye, she lets Daughter fatally
shoot her in the heart, or CPU, at least.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:35.080
Just like that, Daughter has earned her independence.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:40.050
Back at the beach, the woman, alone again,
doodles a picture of Daughter.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:43.550
It's only then that she finds a blinking red
tracking device that Mother has previously

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.560
been seen building and slipping into her bag.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:49.960
Upon discovering the device, she is promptly
cornered by yet another of Mother's bodies.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:53.600
It is chillingly implied that the woman is
not just a useful idiot for Mother's machinations,

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:58.210
but a creation of Mother herself, lab-grown
and micromanaged just as much as Daughter

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:58.700
has been.

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:02.740
Perhaps she was even among the first people
Mother raised from the embryo stores 38 years

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:03.240
ago.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.900
"His parents found me as a baby, orphaned.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.620
Raised me as their own."

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:14.280
"Tell me, do you remember your mother?

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:18.980
Curious, isn't it?"

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.580
It seems that the woman’s arrival to the
facility didn't interrupt Daughter's exam,

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:26.490
but was actually a key part of it, with Mother
pulling the levers this whole time from behind

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:28.410
the curtain like a regular Wizard of Oz.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:31.080
"You don’t feel that every human has intrinsic
value?

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:33.759
And an equal right to life and happiness?"

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:34.980
"I did last month."

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.900
The woman played her role to perfection, and
now that Daughter has passed her exam, and

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:43.160
taken over control of repopulation, her continuing
existence is unnecessary.

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:48.100
I Am Mother ends with Daughter back where
she started, but with her situation completely

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:48.600
changed.

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.980
She's learned the truth about Mother, to a
certain extent, and knows she cannot trust

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:52.480
her.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.660
But she's also now experienced and been lied
to by the outside world.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:58.720
As Blink-182 once put it, "I guess this is
growing up."

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.280
"That was an attempt at humor."

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.840
Though her journey with the woman was short,
it was immensely consequential.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:10.600
Daughter’s become a wiser person who's learned
to trust herself, not the outside world, nor

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:12.020
the robot who raised her.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:16.329
According to director Grant Sputore, that
process of forging one’s own path is what

00:09:16.329 --> 00:09:17.410
the movie is really about.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:20.139
"Is a discussion of what it means to be a
good person.

00:09:20.139 --> 00:09:21.899
How do you work out right from wrong?

00:09:21.899 --> 00:09:26.370
How do you work out who you are, separate
to what your parents want you to be, or what

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:29.840
religion's told you to do, or what you read
in a book sometime?"

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.500
She'll pass this wisdom on to her brother,
a helpless child whom she’s now determined

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:34.000
to raise.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.720
It's a development that recontextualizes the
story you've been watching, right down to

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.280
its title.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.520
She's the mother now.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:42.699
Make no mistake, though, this is far from
an empowering ending.

00:09:42.699 --> 00:09:46.499
In killing and replacing Mother, she is only
fulfilling Mother’s master plan of creating

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.700
a newer, better version of the human race.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.800
She feels independent, but she’s not.

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:52.569
This was all a part of Mother’s plan.

00:09:52.569 --> 00:09:56.420
As the movie comes to a close, Daughter regards
the thousands of remaining embryos in the

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:59.020
facility, preparing for the daunting task
ahead.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.940
Mother as she knows her is gone, but her plan
lives on.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:05.179
No matter what Daughter does next, she will
always be her Mother's child.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:08.780
"Your brother is the first of many, Daughter.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:11.220
Soon, we'll welcome more."

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.740
